  {
    "subject": "mechanical",
    "question": "Explain a piston, cylinder and piston rod to a beginner in English. Use the supported 3D piston and highlight the rod as you explain it. Explain which parts move, without pretending to run an engine simulation. Keep the lesson to four short teaching chunks including one understanding question.",
    "elapsed_seconds": 5.01,
    "fallback_attempted": false,
    "errors": [],
    "answer": {
      "chunks": [
        {
          "speak": "Imagine a hollow tube, like a can that's open at both ends. This is called a cylinder. Inside this cylinder, there's a disc-shaped part that fits snugly, called a piston. The piston can slide up and down within the cylinder.",
          "diagram": {
            "action": "none",
            "visual": {
              "kind": "assembly",
              "model": "piston",
              "focus": "cylinder",
              "phase": 0.5
            }
          },
          "key_point": "Piston and Cylinder"
        },
        {
          "speak": "Attached to the piston is a long, thin shaft called the piston rod. The rod extends out from the cylinder and is used to transfer the motion of the piston to other parts of a machine.",
          "diagram": {
            "action": "highlight",
            "visual": {
              "kind": "assembly",
              "model": "piston",
              "focus": "rod",
              "phase": 0.5
            }
          },
          "key_point": "Piston Rod"
        },
        {
          "speak": "In this setup, the cylinder usually stays still. The piston is the part that moves back and forth inside the cylinder, and because the piston rod is attached to it, the rod also moves back and forth along with the piston.",
          "diagram": {
            "action": "highlight",
            "visual": {
              "kind": "assembly",
              "model": "piston",
              "focus": "piston",
              "phase": 0.5
            }
          },
          "key_point": "Parts in Motion"
        },
        {
          "question": "Out of the three parts we discussed\u2014the piston, the cylinder, and the piston rod\u2014which two parts typically move?",
          "expected_concepts": [
            "piston",
            "piston rod",
            "movement"
          ],
          "speak": "Out of the three parts we discussed\u2014the piston, the cylinder, and the piston rod\u2014which two parts typically move?",
          "diagram": {
